{"title":"2018 USAMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/3/d733ecc66816357f752d29fbb46ef643c318a8a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:(0,\\infty) \\to (0,\\infty)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"155\" height=\"20\" /> such that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/4/8945fb40f421318fdb191894bc65db33f0253cd0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f\\left(x+\\frac{1}{y}\\right)+f\\left(y+\\frac{1}{z}\\right) + f\\left(z+\\frac{1}{x}\\right) = 1\\]\" width=\"333\" height=\"43\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/7/2977f3b8dac09821205b23be7a5aabe6e959e5d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z &gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/a/f2a2c5e8287e4a17962a54003036fbdd661c8d57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz =1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Obviously, the output of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> lies in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be11a56a55425d6c6b69f70f5fa98eab95e8ad18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/8/53834df9c386d7d9d06da375158f57c3b7e2b257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g:(0,1)\\to(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"20\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/5/135faedef4201e6cd6dd6884fe7fc866f5ce5052.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)=f\\left(\\frac1x-1\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"146\" height=\"45\" />. Then for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d894f19f565c1d84e828ac790456d59b242907d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c\\in(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/6/0463a97b25dc0b519ce3c0a1ba6ff2ab6f9f518f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/1/b01f37aa4d3b16f739203db2d46d376f6f968de8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(a)=f\\left(\\frac1a-1\\right)=f\\left(\\frac{1-a}a\\right)=f\\left(\\frac{b+c}a\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"359\" height=\"45\" />. We can transform <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/d/74d7137f504b048a37da48667ce9de32fccf9bcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/5/585c270af261665f917c93a1412dd8550cce5926.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"33\" height=\"20\" /> similarly:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/6/086a179e85c91c54c14d93410de872bb14de1f94.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g(a)+g(b)+g(c)=f\\left(\\frac ca+\\frac ba\\right)+f\\left(\\frac ab+\\frac cb\\right)+f\\left(\\frac bc+\\frac ac\\right)\\]\" width=\"465\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/5/115c774d825c598758e9c22f527ca62b708f5c85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac ca$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"34\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/8/20808004a0151f91f1c291fb52090ed8e8f0b899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"49\" height=\"34\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/f/abf6d1bf66bf056600b992349a5f64970e112c44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=\\frac bc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"47\" height=\"39\" />. We can see that the above expression is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. That is, for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d894f19f565c1d84e828ac790456d59b242907d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c\\in(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/6/0463a97b25dc0b519ce3c0a1ba6ff2ab6f9f518f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/4/e744ab593ee82662135e7516f3ac7e72b888abdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(a)+g(b)+g(c)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>(To motivate this, one can start by writing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/e/69e08a2922403a11656aff073bd6d388f30775f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"34\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/a/29a015f5759c5c36fd88290af66c32923ff9ad5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac bc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"47\" height=\"39\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/d/eadc07a75aa9d3c0406c219f6d9383b5ddb90cf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=\\frac ca$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"45\" height=\"33\" />, and normalizing such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/6/0463a97b25dc0b519ce3c0a1ba6ff2ab6f9f518f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" />.)\n</p><p><br />\nFor convenience, we define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/995d260ffc47f08862be2c4c29600dc1ecf6fb56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h:\\left(-\\frac13,\\frac23\\right)\\to\\left(-\\frac13,\\frac23\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"205\" height=\"45\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/0/8e0041762f1e5a7a37954bff9a0a851606099843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(x)=g\\left(x+\\frac13\\right)-\\frac13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"181\" height=\"45\" />, so that for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8eb36fd55cfebc6674bf82bdb2289feec3cb344.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c\\in\\left(-\\frac13,\\frac23\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"140\" height=\"45\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37e4c3e85710cff4f69bfec2adaff5ea38111a3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" />, we have \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/1/c81866e6f6715bfaac33a9bccd26cfe64b665ace.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[h(a)+h(b)+h(c)=g\\left(a+\\frac13\\right)-\\frac13+g\\left(b+\\frac13\\right)-\\frac13+g\\left(c+\\frac13\\right)-\\frac13=1-1=0.\\]\" width=\"601\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Obviously, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f77a1bc5df30224829588fa441a3459bbb90f2d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(0)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/978c2d670426a65881478463c63bf80824addba4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a|&lt;\\frac13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/7/127abebc92377030dc908cc36e31a091a31d58d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(a)+h(-a)+h(0)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"196\" height=\"20\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/8/55845da105375032868bc03a8536697d41218c7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(-a)=-h(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"123\" height=\"20\" />. Furthermore, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> are in the domain and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/5/dc5d3838b6a92e82dc05641886ab8df8fd912725.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a+b|&lt;\\frac13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/2/7121c123d2759d246bc4dcb4a1a5b71ad89095b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(a)+h(b)+h(-(a+b))=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"239\" height=\"20\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/7507fbbfb544cac9473c12428a3255f83b3d5bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(a+b)=h(a)+h(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p><br />\nAt this point, we should realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> should be of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/1017c7baa918c48d8a65eb013c3d9dd3bfbaedce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(x)=kx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" />. We first prove this for some rational numbers. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a real number such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/1/3918987280fcc7e8dbe1ef08d1ba294b27a0c8b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|nx|&lt;\\frac13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"71\" height=\"38\" />, then we can repeatedly apply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/7507fbbfb544cac9473c12428a3255f83b3d5bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(a+b)=h(a)+h(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" /> to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be29e6ea68839965a3a64f365b3e91dbbf4a3feb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(nx)=nh(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/d/e4dbf5af432ba0325e0139685e0ac3ca7f9e8337.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=6h\\left(\\frac16\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"98\" height=\"45\" />, then for any rational number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/c/e9c424abbd10971d03ee96f9d74bb12a31d74068.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\frac pq\\in\\left(0,\\frac13\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"127\" height=\"45\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f779d95c15f7e41de74cb767f52fe4e7b92c745e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p,q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> are positive integers, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/f/e9f63e9d9d97b2a8553fbbf8aea15ad9353d23c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(r)=6p*h\\left(\\frac1{6q}\\right)=\\frac{6p}q*h\\left(\\frac16\\right)=kr$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"316\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Next, we prove it for all real numbers in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/6/046b7fa74789b43ac7ed48be81f9a3865f671ab2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(0,\\frac13\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"58\" height=\"45\" />. For the sake of contradiction, assume that there is some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/0/300d88360be05d587704b9ff132cd5748a42ec6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in\\left(0,\\frac13\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"91\" height=\"45\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/915b56100e4897cbcaee431b1b25c05e90b43c78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(x)\\ne kx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/f/acf3b7f66328237e4c38dc29ce879052e38da8e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E=h(x)-kx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />, then obviously <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/a/45afd36ec580eefc9dccf8abe9dc7bd72d7d111c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;|E|&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" />. The idea is to \"amplify\" this error until it becomes so big as to contradict the bounds on the output of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/0/9a05ce986d8d1048eaa48b7e0a2d937d11d79f5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=\\left\\lceil\\frac1{|E|}\\right\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"92\" height=\"45\" />, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/1/2d1f102631d4be45ca9a6678e7758660c039265e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N\\ge2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/3/b93bfa835255c126e1a4201ec2073d236c27f2a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|NE|\\ge1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" />. Pick any rational <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa07357020079856cff6a01b4c7a2f0881ab21b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r\\in\\left(\\frac{N-1}Nx,x\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"140\" height=\"45\" />, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d8ae243e451541ced200dd9faecdc5fe33daed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0&lt;x-r&lt;N(x-r)&lt;x&lt;\\frac13.\\]\" width=\"246\" height=\"37\" />\nAll numbers and sums are safely inside the bounds of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4ccf5278661e902b8db710b8e450bca94233133.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(-\\frac13,\\frac13\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"76\" height=\"45\" />. Thus\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/0/c40a613358f68dca21132442b6b8999de61a2f9b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[h(N(x-r))=Nh(x-r)=N(h(x)+h(-r))=N(h(x)-h(r))=kN(x-r)+NE,\\]\" width=\"623\" height=\"18\" />\nbut picking any rational number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a7badc39eba3dd4087f8e797444b6df343a448c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\in\\left(N(x-r),\\frac13\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"152\" height=\"45\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/4/8f4184012bd39d49469e7fd41ae2df10489c9939.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|kN(x-r)|&lt;|ks|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"147\" height=\"20\" />, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d82678c7d7b7c7b2c1d1a071f11723e30e78463.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ks=h(s)\\in\\left(-\\frac13,\\frac23\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"175\" height=\"45\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/5/775c96e84672e48dfd78aab5071f50d700f29bfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$kN(x-r)\\in\\left(-\\frac13,\\frac23\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"181\" height=\"45\" /> as well, but since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/d/3ddf605eca27201755b59a2dd2e9e57d38877e28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$NE\\ge1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"17\" />, this means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/4/ef480d994ddc307e9c5b5f679848ce538cd4cb9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(N(x-r))=kN(x-r)+NE\\notin\\left(-\\frac13,\\frac23\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"355\" height=\"45\" />, giving us the desired contradiction.\n</p><p><br />\nWe now know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/1017c7baa918c48d8a65eb013c3d9dd3bfbaedce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(x)=kx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/d/6edf7e64ed8d1af8bb73295c01f038486445dc1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x&lt;\\frac13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"38\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/a/83a540e4a13166a5746914f0c889d7bad99bee45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(-x)=-h(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/5/af579175d620eed738d49a26021cb28c8a5a97c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x|&lt;\\frac13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"60\" height=\"38\" />, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/1017c7baa918c48d8a65eb013c3d9dd3bfbaedce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(x)=kx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/5/af579175d620eed738d49a26021cb28c8a5a97c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x|&lt;\\frac13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"60\" height=\"38\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/a/08a893a0b29ee993b79127264b551fad7a2c640a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in\\left(\\frac13,\\frac23\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"95\" height=\"45\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/b/89bc80810bcd4e65e1ced9add22e037343e8c3dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(x)+h\\left(-\\frac x2\\right)+h\\left(-\\frac x2\\right)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"241\" height=\"35\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/1017c7baa918c48d8a65eb013c3d9dd3bfbaedce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(x)=kx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" /> as well. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/1017c7baa918c48d8a65eb013c3d9dd3bfbaedce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(x)=kx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in the domain. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/7/1f745cf4286f88b236750e1e9a8abe3dacd9dc39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> is bounded by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/b/9cbd60d7eb44ab3db2aa6af763eda8e99d2eccdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/1/611d08a8c57a214b2b964bba16da8157a5b81c9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/8/1386b0b028379ac0d896c65eb49f31e3725adaa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac12\\le k\\le1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" />. It remains to work backwards to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/0/e10577a4987db1fa09a52054832a07904d6cfcda.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} h(x) &amp;= kx \\\\ g(x) &amp;= kx+\\frac{1-k}3 \\\\ f(x) &amp;= \\frac k{1+x}+\\frac{1-k}3\\quad\\left(-\\frac12\\le k\\le1\\right). \\end{align*}\" width=\"319\" height=\"113\" />\n- wzs26843545602\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO\" title=\"2018 USAMO\">2018 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2018\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2018 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018005714\nCache expiry: 86400\n